# Security headers for Cloudflare Pages (static assets + prerendered pages).
# NOTE: Pages applies _headers to STATIC responses only — /api/weather (a
# Pages Function) does not get these; set headers in its Response objects
# in src/pages/api/weather.ts if ever needed (low value: consumed via
# fetch().json(), params numerically range-checked).
#
# HSTS: header ships now; the hstspreload.org SUBMISSION is deliberately
# held until we're sure no plain-http subdomain of waxup.app will ever be
# needed (submission is hard to undo; the header alone is reversible).
#
# Post-launch TODO: Content-Security-Policy — ship as
# Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only first (inline module scripts + the
# is:inline reveal gate need script-src 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self'
# is enough — the browser only calls same-origin /api/weather).
#
# Permissions-Policy MUST keep geolocation=(self): the Active Weather chip
# calls navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition (WaterSurface.astro).

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
